request.description:
Server-Sent Events (SSE) endpoint for live patient display queue updates. Automatically detects current IST time. Updates are pushed in real-time when:
- New patient is added to queue
- Patient status changes (Scheduled → In Progress → Completed)
- Visit is updated or cancelled
- Date changes (auto-switches to new day)

Uses readable doctorId (e.g., DOC00001) instead of MongoDB ObjectId.

**Token Numbering:** Separate sequences per doctor per day:
- Emergency visits: 1, 2, 3... (separate sequence)
- Regular visits (New, Follow-up, MR): 1, 2, 3... (separate sequence)
- Both reset at 12 AM IST
- Frontend should display Emergency tokens with E- prefix based on visitType

Frontend Usage:
```javascript
const eventSource = new EventSource('/api/v1/hospital/visits/display/stream/DOC00001');

eventSource.onmessage = (event) => {
  const data = JSON.parse(event.data);
  console.log('Event type:', data.type);
  console.log('Queue:', data.queue);
  updateDisplay(data);
};

eventSource.onerror = (error) => {
  console.error('SSE error:', error);
  eventSource.close();
};
```

Event Types:
- initial: First data sent on connection
- status-change: Visit status updated
- new-visit: New patient added
- visit-updated: Visit details changed
- visit-deleted: Visit cancelled/deleted
- date-change: Date changed (auto-detected)
- queue-refresh: Full queue refresh

